$ bof3 --version
[exit 0]
bof3 1.0.0

$ bof3 disc --help
[exit 0]
bof3 disc: read, extract, checksum, rebuild and verify a PlayStation disc image.

Usage: bof3 disc <COMMAND> [OPTIONS]
       bof3 disc <COMMAND> --help

Commands:
  extract   write every file of an image, plus its project XML
  lba-json  write the LBA table of an extracted tree
  checksum  hash the .bin, .cue, .img and .iso files below a folder
  verify    compare those files with their checksums; exit 1 on a mismatch
  rebuild   build a synthetic ISO from top-level files

Every command has focused help: bof3 disc <COMMAND> --help.
Common switches: -i/--input PATH, -o/--output PATH, -q/--quiet.

Examples:
  bof3 disc extract -i "Breath of Fire III (USA).cue" -o build/disc
  bof3 disc checksum -i dumps -o build/checksums.json
  bof3 disc verify -i dumps -o build/checksums.json

$ bof3 disc extract --help
[exit 0]
bof3 disc extract: write every file of an image, plus its project XML.

Usage: bof3 disc extract [-i IMAGE.cue] [-o DIR] [-p FILE.xml] [-q]

  -i, --input PATH    disc image or .cue sheet (default: the image in
                      inputs/external, then ./disk)
  -o, --output DIR    folder to extract into (default: build/extracted)
  -p, --project FILE  project XML to write (default: DIR/IMAGE.xml)
  -q, --quiet         no completion line (default: off)

Examples:
  bof3 disc extract -i "Breath of Fire III (USA).cue" -o build/disc
  bof3 disc extract -q

$ bof3 disc lba-json --help
[exit 0]
bof3 disc lba-json: write the LBA table of an extracted tree.

Usage: bof3 disc lba-json -i IMAGE -o FILE.json -x DIR -p FILE.xml [-r DIR] [-q]

  -i, --input PATH    disc image or .cue sheet (required)
  -o, --output FILE   JSON table to write (required)
  -x, --extract DIR   extraction folder the table describes (required)
  -p, --project FILE  project XML of that extraction (required)
  -r, --raw-root DIR  archive root (default: processed/emi_raw)
  -q, --quiet         no completion line (default: off)

Example:
  bof3 disc lba-json -i game.cue -o build/lba.json -x build/disc -p build/disc/game.xml

$ bof3 disc checksum --help
[exit 0]
bof3 disc checksum: hash the .bin, .cue, .img and .iso files below a folder.

Usage: bof3 disc checksum -i DIR -o FILE.json [-q]

  -i, --input DIR     folder that holds the disc dump (required)
  -o, --output FILE   JSON checksums to write (required)
  -q, --quiet         no completion line (default: off)

Example:
  bof3 disc checksum -i dumps -o build/checksums.json

$ bof3 disc verify --help
[exit 0]
bof3 disc verify: compare the .bin, .cue, .img and .iso files below a folder with their checksums.

Usage: bof3 disc verify -i DIR -o FILE.json [-q]

  -i, --input DIR     folder that holds the disc dump (required)
  -o, --output FILE   JSON checksums to compare against (required)
  -q, --quiet         no completion line (default: off)

Exit status: 0 every file matches, 1 a mismatch, 2 an error.

Example:
  bof3 disc verify -i dumps -o build/checksums.json

$ bof3 disc rebuild --help
[exit 0]
bof3 disc rebuild: build a synthetic ISO from top-level files.

Usage: bof3 disc rebuild -i DIR -o IMAGE.iso [-q]

  -i, --input DIR     folder whose top-level files go in the image (required)
  -o, --output FILE   ISO to write (required)
  -q, --quiet         no completion line (default: off)

Example:
  bof3 disc rebuild -i build/iso-files -o build/synthetic.iso

$ bof3 emi --help
[exit 0]
bof3 emi: list, extract, pack and inspect EMI archives.

Usage: bof3 emi <COMMAND> [OPTIONS]
       bof3 emi ARCHIVE.EMI [OPTIONS]     extract it

Commands:
  extract   write every entry of an archive, or one entry, as files
  pack      build an archive from a folder or from named files
  list      show the entry table, as text or JSON
  vram      decode the type-3 VRAM uploads into one page set
  clut      decode one CLUT palette entry
  vab       parse one VAB sound bank entry
  sep       parse one sequence package entry
  coverage  check which formats rebuild their own bytes

Every command has focused help: bof3 emi <COMMAND> --help.
Common switches: -i/--input PATH, -o/--output PATH, -q/--quiet.

Examples:
  bof3 emi list "BIN/BGM/BGM000.EMI"
  bof3 emi extract -i "BIN/BGM/BGM000.EMI" -o build/bgm000
  bof3 emi pack -o build/test.EMI build/src

$ bof3 emi extract --help
[exit 0]
bof3 emi extract: write every entry of an archive, or one entry, as files.

Usage: bof3 emi extract [-i ARCHIVE] [-o DIR|FILE] [-n INDEX] [-e] [-J [FILE]] [-d] [-q]

  -i, --input ARCHIVE       archive to read (or pass it as the only positional)
  -o, --output PATH         DIR for every entry, FILE for one INDEX
                            (default: the archive name without .EMI)
  -n, --index INDEX         write only this entry (default: every entry)
      --extensions, -e      add each entry's format extension (default: off)
  -J, --manifest-json [FILE]
                            also write emi.json (default: DIR/emi.json); a bare -J
                            must be last, because the next argument is its path
  -d, --dry-run             write nothing (default: off)
  -q, --quiet               no completion line (default: off)

Examples:
  bof3 emi extract -i "BIN/BGM/BGM000.EMI" -o build/bgm000
  bof3 emi extract -i "BIN/BGM/BGM000.EMI" -n 3 -e -o build/one
  bof3 emi extract -i "BIN/BGM/BGM000.EMI" -o build/bgm000 -J

$ bof3 emi pack --help
[exit 0]
bof3 emi pack: build an EMI archive from a folder, or from named files.

Usage: bof3 emi pack -o ARCHIVE.EMI [-i FILE...] | FOLDER [OPTIONS]

  -i, --input FILE...       files to pack, in order (default: use FOLDER)
  -o, --output ARCHIVE.EMI  archive to write (required)
  -t, --type TYPE           file type for inputs whose extension names none
                            (default: 255)
  -I, --include PATTERN     folder files to include (default: every file)
  -X, --exclude PATTERN     folder files to exclude (default: emi.json)
  -J, --manifest-json [FILE]
                            read emi.json instead of guessing types
                            (default: FOLDER/emi.json)
  -k, --keep-original       keep the input files (default)
  -K, --no-keep             delete the inputs after the archive is written
  -d, --dry-run             write nothing (default: off)
  -q, --quiet               no completion line (default: off)

Examples:
  bof3 emi pack -o build/test.EMI -i header.vh body.vb
  bof3 emi pack -o build/test.EMI -X '*.md' build/src

$ bof3 emi list --help
[exit 0]
bof3 emi list: show an archive's entry table.

Usage: bof3 emi list [-i ARCHIVE] [--json]

  -i, --input ARCHIVE  archive to read (or pass it as the only positional)
      --json           print one JSON object per entry, as a JSON array
                       (default: a text table)

Examples:
  bof3 emi list "BIN/BGM/BGM000.EMI"
  bof3 emi list -i "BIN/BGM/BGM000.EMI" --json

